        detailedAnswer: 'Use `TriggerRule.ONE_FAILED` for a notification task: even if upstream succeeds, the alert task stays dormant; if any upstream fails, the alert fires. `TriggerRule.ALL_DONE` runs regardless of upstream status — use for cleanup tasks that must always run (e.g., releasing a lock). `TriggerRule.NONE_FAILED_MIN_ONE_SUCCESS` is useful for parallel fanout with optional branches.',
