        q: 'What is watermarking in Spark Structured Streaming?',
        a: 'Watermarking handles late-arriving data by defining how long to wait for late events. Example: withWatermark("timestamp", "10 minutes") tells Spark to keep state for events up to 10 minutes late. After the threshold, late records are dropped. Without watermarks, streaming state grows unbounded.',
        detailedAnswer: '`df.withWatermark("event_time", "10 minutes").groupBy(window("event_time", "5 minutes"), "user_id").count()` — Spark tracks the max event_time seen so far (the "watermark"). State for a window is held until watermark > window end + delay threshold. After that, the window result is finalized and state is dropped. Trade-off: longer watermark = more late data captured but more state (memory). Monitor state size via Spark UI Structured Streaming tab.',
