        q: 'What is Microsoft Fabric and how does it differ from Azure Synapse Analytics?',
        a: 'Fabric is a unified SaaS analytics platform that brings Lakehouses, Warehouses, notebooks, pipelines, event streaming, semantic models, and Power BI into one governed OneLake workspace. Synapse is still a better fit when you need mature dedicated SQL pool workloads, tighter infrastructure control, or an existing enterprise estate that is cheaper to keep than migrate.',
        detailedAnswer: 'Use Fabric when you want one product experience for engineering and BI, less infrastructure overhead, and faster time to insight. Use Synapse when you need more control over compute, networking, or a large pre-existing dedicated SQL pool. Fabric trades some low-level control for simplicity: storage, orchestration, and BI live in one capacity, so you must monitor shared usage carefully. From a governance view, Fabric centralizes identity, workspace permissions, and Purview lineage; from a cost/performance view, OneLake plus Direct Lake can reduce copy and refresh cost, but only if Gold tables are compact and the semantic model is well designed. A common interview mistake is calling Fabric "just Synapse with a new UI" instead of explaining the OneLake and Direct Lake architecture change.',
