        detailedAnswer: 'A strong answer should show when Fabric wins and when Synapse still wins. Fabric wins when the team wants one SaaS platform for engineering, serving, and BI with less orchestration overhead. Synapse wins when the organization values fine-grained control, already owns a heavily tuned dedicated SQL pool, or needs to keep a known enterprise pattern stable while they modernize incrementally. Tradeoff wise, Fabric reduces platform sprawl and copy operations, but shared capacity means Spark, SQL, and BI can contend for the same resources. Governance is simpler in Fabric, while Synapse can fit organizations that prefer a more explicit separation of storage, compute, and BI. Cost/performance-wise, Fabric can be cheaper to operate for new estates, but you still need to size and monitor capacity carefully. Common mistake: answering this as a product preference question instead of a workload and operating-model question.',
