        q: 'Your Fabric Lakehouse Delta table has 500,000 small files after 6 months of streaming writes. How do you fix this and prevent recurrence?',
        a: 'Fix: run OPTIMIZE on the Delta table to compact small files into 1GB Parquet files. Run VACUUM to remove old file versions beyond the retention period. Prevent: configure Structured Streaming checkpointing with trigger intervals (not continuous), enable Delta auto-compaction (delta.autoOptimize.autoCompact=true) and optimized writes (delta.autoOptimize.optimizeWrite=true) at the table level.',
        detailedAnswer: 'Small file problem: each Spark micro-batch with 10K events writes 1 small Parquet file. After 6 months × 24 batches/hour = 43,200 files. Reading 43K files has massive overhead: each file requires a separate read task, metadata scan is slow, and Parquet statistics are fragmented. Fix: `OPTIMIZE silver.events ZORDER BY (event_date, user_id)` — compacts all files into optimally sized 1GB files and ZORDERs for query performance. This takes 20-60 min for 500K files but pays off immediately in query speed. Prevention: `ALTER TABLE silver.events SET TBLPROPERTIES (\'delta.autoOptimize.autoCompact\' = \'true\', \'delta.autoOptimize.optimizeWrite\' = \'true\')` — these make every write operation produce larger files and automatically compact small files after each write. Also: run OPTIMIZE + VACUUM weekly via a scheduled Fabric Pipeline as table maintenance.',
