        detailedAnswer: 'KQL vs SQL vs Spark for streaming: (1) KQL Database ingests millions of events/second, answers "events in last 5 minutes by device" in <100ms via its columnar store and native time-series indexing. SQL cannot match this on the same data volume. (2) Databricks Structured Streaming can run arbitrary Python/Spark logic but has 5-30 second micro-batch latency vs. KQL\'s sub-second. (3) Azure Stream Analytics is a simpler SQL-based streaming engine — lower learning curve, less powerful than Structured Streaming or KQL. Production pattern: Event Hub → Eventstream → KQL Database (real-time alerts, dashboards) + Lakehouse Delta (batch analytics, ML training data). This dual-path handles both sub-second alerting and historical analysis from the same ingestion pipeline.',
