        a: 'Ingest: Kafka (partitioned by device_id) or Event Hubs/Kinesis for managed option. Stream processing: Spark Structured Streaming or Flink for real-time aggregations (1-minute device averages). Batch layer: daily Spark job for complex ML features. Storage: Delta Lake on cloud storage (partitioned by date + device_region). Serving: Aggregates in a fast query layer (Redshift/Synapse/BigQuery); raw in cold storage. Monitoring: consumer lag alerts, SLA checks on batch job completion.',
        detailedAnswer: 'Scale calculation: 10B events/day = ~115K events/second average. Kafka sizing: 12 partitions × 10K events/sec/partition = 120K events/sec capacity. Storage: at 200 bytes/event, raw storage = 2 TB/day. After Parquet compression (~10:1): 200 GB/day. Partition layout: `s3://lake/events/date=2024-01-15/region=us-west/` — queries always filter by date. Retention: raw 90 days (18 TB), aggregated forever. Hot path latency target: < 5 seconds end-to-end (ingest → dashboard). Cold path: batch job completes within 2 hours of midnight UTC.',
