        detailedAnswer: 'The producer should publish the contract, communicate breaking changes in advance, and provide a compatibility window. The consumer should declare which fields, freshness windows, and semantic rules it depends on. In practice, I would store the contract alongside the source metadata, validate it in CI, and make the release fail if the producer is about to break an agreed-upon guarantee.',
        scenario: 'An app team changes a payload field from `customer_name` to `full_name` and the analytics team depends on the old field in downstream models.',
